IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sga1-classes`

-- Tests for sga1-classes.l4 (ss 74 to 75). Every expected value is written from the text of the section, beside the assertion.
-- Arguments are positional, in the order of each function's GIVEN.

§ `Section 74: rights of holders of classes of shares`

-- (1) Arguments: share capital divided into classes; provision in the constitution for variation; the constitution specifies (a)(i) consent as necessary; the constitution specifies (a)(ii) a separate-meeting resolution as necessary;
-- the consent has been given; the separate-meeting resolution has sanctioned it; the percentage of the class held by those who sanctioned it by resolution.
-- (a)(i) specified and met: the exception is met, so the variation is not barred
#ASSERT `s 74(1) the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the class is barred` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a)(i) specified and not met
#ASSERT `s 74(1) the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the class is barred` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a)(ii) specified and met; not met
#ASSERT `s 74(1) the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the class is barred` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74(1) the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the class is barred` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- both specified as necessary: each is necessary (fork F-CL1)
#ASSERT `s 74(1) the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the class is barred` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74(1) the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the class is barred` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): the constitution specifies neither: a resolution of holders in total of not less than 75 per cent
#ASSERT `s 74(1) the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the class is barred` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 75 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74(1) the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the class is barred` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74(1) the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the class is barred` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 74 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) is not available where the constitution specifies one of the matters in (a)
#ASSERT `s 74(1) the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the class is barred` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 90 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the company's share capital is not divided into classes, or the constitution makes no provision: not covered
#ASSERT `s 74(1) the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the class is barred` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 74(1) the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the class is barred` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 74(1) a company must not vary or abrogate the rights attached to a class of shares except as the subsection allows` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 74(1) vary or abrogate the rights attached to a class of shares otherwise than as the subsection allows` AT 1

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 74(1) a company must not vary or abrogate the rights attached to a class of shares except as the subsection allows` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH

-- (1AA) Arguments: the rights have been varied or abrogated in accordance with subsection (1); the percentage of the class held by the applicants, treasury shares disregarded.
#ASSERT `s 74(1AA) the holders may apply to the Court to have the variation or abrogation cancelled` TRUE 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74(1AA) the holders may apply to the Court to have the variation or abrogation cancelled` TRUE 12.5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- under 5 per cent: the text does not say they may not
#ASSERT `s 74(1AA) the holders may apply to the Court to have the variation or abrogation cancelled` TRUE 4 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 74(1AA) the holders may apply to the Court to have the variation or abrogation cancelled` FALSE 50 EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1AB) Arguments: an application has been made to the Court; the Court has confirmed the variation or abrogation.
#ASSERT `s 74(1AB) the variation or abrogation has not yet taken effect` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74(1AB) the variation or abrogation has not yet taken effect` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74(1AB) the variation or abrogation has not yet taken effect` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1A) Argument: the share is held as a treasury share.
#ASSERT `s 74(1A) the share is disregarded for the purposes of subsections (1) and (1AA)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74(1A) the share is disregarded for the purposes of subsections (1) and (1AA)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: the shares held by the holders in question; the total issued shares of the class; the shares held as treasury shares.
#ASSERT `s 74(1A) the percentage of the total number of shares of the class held by the holders, treasury shares disregarded, in per cent` 10 100 0 EQUALS JUST 10
-- 10 of 100 shares with 50 held as treasury shares: 10 of the 50 that count, which is 20 per cent
#ASSERT `s 74(1A) the percentage of the total number of shares of the class held by the holders, treasury shares disregarded, in per cent` 10 100 50 EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `s 74(1A) the percentage of the total number of shares of the class held by the holders, treasury shares disregarded, in per cent` 0 100 50 EQUALS JUST 0
-- no share left to count
#ASSERT `s 74(1A) the percentage of the total number of shares of the class held by the holders, treasury shares disregarded, in per cent` 0 50 50 EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2) Arguments: the applicants or any of them consented to or voted in favour; the Court is satisfied that a material fact was not disclosed.
#ASSERT `s 74(2) the application is invalid by reason of the applicants having consented to or voted in favour of the resolution` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- consented and no non-disclosure shown: the subsection does not say
#ASSERT `s 74(2) the application is invalid by reason of the applicants having consented to or voted in favour of the resolution` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 74(2) the application is invalid by reason of the applicants having consented to or voted in favour of the resolution` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3) Arguments: the day the consent was given or the resolution was passed; the application has been made; the day it was made; the Court allows further time; the last day of the further time; the day on which the question is asked.
-- consent given on 1 March 2026: one month after is 1 April 2026
#ASSERT `s 74(3) the application is out of time` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74(3) the application is out of time` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 2 4 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "such further time as the Court allows"
#ASSERT `s 74(3) the application is out of time` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 2 4 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74(3) the application is out of time` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 5 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no application yet
#ASSERT `s 74(3) the application is out of time` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74(3) the application is out of time` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 2 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74(3) the application is out of time` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 2 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74(3) the application is out of time` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- on behalf of the shareholders, by those they appoint in writing
#ASSERT `s 74(3) the application may be made on behalf of the shareholders entitled to make it by those they appoint` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74(3) the application may be made on behalf of the shareholders entitled to make it by those they appoint` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (4) Arguments: an application has been made; the Court is satisfied that the variation or abrogation would unfairly prejudice the shareholders of the class represented by the applicant.
#ASSERT `s 74(4) the Court may disallow the variation or abrogation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "must, if not so satisfied, confirm it"
#ASSERT `s 74(4) the Court may disallow the variation or abrogation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74(4) the Court may disallow the variation or abrogation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 74(4) the Court must confirm the variation or abrogation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74(4) the Court must confirm the variation or abrogation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74(4) the Court must confirm the variation or abrogation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "the decision of the Court is final"
#ASSERT `s 74(4) the decision of the Court is final` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74(4) the decision of the Court is final` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (5) Arguments: the Court has made an order on an application; the day the order was made; a copy has been lodged; the day it was lodged; the day on which the question is asked.
-- an order made on 1 March 2026: the 14th day is 15 March 2026
#ASSERT `s 74(5) the company is late in lodging a copy of the order with the Registrar` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74(5) the company is late in lodging a copy of the order with the Registrar` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 16 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74(5) the company is late in lodging a copy of the order with the Registrar` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74(5) the company is late in lodging a copy of the order with the Registrar` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no order: the duty does not arise
#ASSERT `s 74(5) the company is late in lodging a copy of the order with the Registrar` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 74(5) a company must lodge a copy of the order of the Court with the Registrar within 14 days after the order` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 74(5) lodge a copy of the order of the Court with the Registrar` AT 14

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 74(5) a company must lodge a copy of the order of the Court with the Registrar within 14 days after the order` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 74(5) lodge a copy of the order of the Court with the Registrar` AT 15

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 74(5) a company must lodge a copy of the order of the Court with the Registrar within 14 days after the order` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH

-- the offence: Arguments: default is made in complying with the provision; the person is the company; the person is an officer of the company who is in default.
#ASSERT `s 74(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a fine not exceeding $2,000 "and also to a default penalty" (no amount stated in the subsection)
#ASSERT `s 74(5) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 74(5) penalty` OF 2000, 0, FALSE, TRUE, 0)
#ASSERT `s 74(5) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (6) Arguments: the shares issued are preference shares ranking pari passu with existing preference shares; the issue was authorised by the terms of issue of the existing shares or the constitution then in force.
#ASSERT `s 74(6) the issue is deemed to be a variation of the rights attached to the existing preference shares` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74(6) the issue is deemed to be a variation of the rights attached to the existing preference shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74(6) the issue is deemed to be a variation of the rights attached to the existing preference shares` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (7) Argument: the alteration affects or relates to the manner in which the rights of a class may be varied or abrogated.
#ASSERT `s 74(7) the alteration is deemed to be a variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the shares of the class` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74(7) the alteration is deemed to be a variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the shares of the class` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (8) Argument: the right is a right of a person to obtain relief under section 216.
#ASSERT `s 74(8) section 74 limits or derogates from the right` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74(8) section 74 limits or derogates from the right` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 74A: conversion of shares`

-- (1) Arguments: the share capital is divided into different classes; this section, section 64A or section 75 forbids the provision.
#ASSERT `s 74A(1) the company may make provision in its constitution to authorise the conversion of one class of shares into another class` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74A(1) the company may make provision in its constitution to authorise the conversion of one class of shares into another class` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 74A(1) the company may make provision in its constitution to authorise the conversion of one class of shares into another class` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2) Arguments: public company; the conversion is by special resolution; the constitution permits B to be issued; the constitution sets out the rights attached to B.
#ASSERT `s 74A(2) the public company may convert one class of shares into another class by special resolution` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "only if" both
#ASSERT `s 74A(2) the public company may convert one class of shares into another class by special resolution` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74A(2) the public company may convert one class of shares into another class by special resolution` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74A(2) the public company may convert one class of shares into another class by special resolution` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a private company, or a conversion by another means: not covered
#ASSERT `s 74A(2) the public company may convert one class of shares into another class by special resolution` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 74A(2) the public company may convert one class of shares into another class by special resolution` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3) Arguments: private company; a notice of conversion in the prescribed form has been lodged.
#ASSERT `s 74A(3) the private company may convert shares from one class to another by lodging the notice` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74A(3) the private company may convert shares from one class to another by lodging the notice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 74A(3) the private company may convert shares from one class to another by lodging the notice` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (4) Arguments: private company; the day of the conversion; the register has been updated under section 196A(5).
#ASSERT `s 74A(4) the conversion has not yet taken effect` TRUE (Date 5 3 2016) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74A(4) the conversion has not yet taken effect` TRUE (Date 5 3 2016) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74A(4) the conversion has not yet taken effect` TRUE (Date 2 1 2016) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 74A(4) the conversion has not yet taken effect` FALSE (Date 5 3 2016) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (5) Argument: the conversion involves a variation or an abrogation of the rights attached to a class of shares.
#ASSERT `s 74A(5) section 74 applies to the conversion` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 74A(5) section 74 applies to the conversion` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (6) Argument: the share was a redeemable preference share when it was issued.
#ASSERT `s 74A(6) the share may be converted into a redeemable preference share` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 74A(6) the share may be converted into a redeemable preference share` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 75: rights of holders of preference shares to be set out in the constitution`

-- (1) Arguments: the company allots preference shares or converts issued shares into them; the constitution sets out the rights as to repayment of capital; participation in surplus assets and profits; cumulative or non-cumulative dividends; voting; priority of payment of capital and dividend.
#ASSERT `s 75(1) the company is barred from allotting the preference shares or converting issued shares into them` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 75(1) the company is barred from allotting the preference shares or converting issued shares into them` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75(1) the company is barred from allotting the preference shares or converting issued shares into them` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75(1) the company is barred from allotting the preference shares or converting issued shares into them` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75(1) the company is barred from allotting the preference shares or converting issued shares into them` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75(1) the company is barred from allotting the preference shares or converting issued shares into them` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75(1) the company is barred from allotting the preference shares or converting issued shares into them` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not an allotment of or conversion into preference shares: not covered
#ASSERT `s 75(1) the company is barred from allotting the preference shares or converting issued shares into them` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 75(1) a company must not allot preference shares or convert issued shares into them unless the rights of the holders are set out in the constitution` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 75(1) allot preference shares or convert issued shares into preference shares without setting out the rights of the holders in the constitution` AT 1

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 75(1) a company must not allot preference shares or convert issued shares into them unless the rights of the holders are set out in the constitution` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH

-- (2) Arguments: default is made in complying with the section; the person is the company; the person is an officer of the company who is in default.
#ASSERT `s 75(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 75(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 75(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a fine not exceeding $2,000; no imprisonment; no default penalty
#ASSERT `s 75(2) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 75(2) penalty` OF 2000, 0, FALSE, FALSE, 0)
#ASSERT `s 75(2) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
